  "verdict": "differs",
  "differences": [
    {
      "what": "The small square cupola panel 5 draws at the centre of the blockhouse's cap, under a little four-sided cap of its own, is now built and seated into all four roof planes, and the invented centre stack that stood in its place is gone (count 0). Confirmed by eye against this folder's before/after pair, rendered from the identical camera with only the blockhouse's own bytes changed: before 4b49f0dba271d11ce407e6b407c6e4a766402bce04b93b24ebbcc2862f899e00, after 96d9fb803cdd3b1639c32b9e0c562d0b3bf2af1b2fe8254abea4d62e8e136b15. The cupola's OCCURRENCE is what the picture carries; its size, height, cap pitch and plain sides are reconstructed (docs/LIBERTIES.md L-second-fort-blockhouse-cupola-2388), so this is not a claim that the built cupola is the pictured cupola's measure.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    {
      "what": "The camera is the T-3040 initial landmark fit, reused here unchanged so that the before and after differ only by the blockhouse's bytes. It reached its imposed 100 m eye bound and renders the whole compound aerial and undersized against a nearly level printed view; both stockade endpoints are cropped. It is marked diagnostic_only and is not an accepted historical viewing position. Scale, height and framing still want fitting before anything here is judged pixel for pixel. Nothing was moved to fit it.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "what": "The print shows a galleried range; the corresponding range identity, its galleries, facade openings, roof forms and the other buildings' chimney counts are unresolved. Surveyed placements are not moved to fit a compressed retrospective composition.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "what": "The compound's composition as a whole — the relative sizes and spacing the print draws — differs from the committed survey, and the other dated pictures of the fort listed on T-2388 have not been read against it at all.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "what": "Terrain, bank, river, trees and canoes are excluded from this common-grade analytical renderer; rendered context members are not thereby pictured or attested.",
      "status": "not shown"
    },
    {
      "what": "Colour and tone: the sheet is a chromolithograph whose palette is the printer's, and no source states the colour of any surface of this fort.",
      "status": "not shown"
    }
  ],
  "_how": "verdict is unreviewed | differs | matches, set by whoever compared the side-by-side with the picture; each difference is {what, status: open | fixed | not shown | within tolerance | owner ruling} — open only if a street visitor would notice it (over about 1 ft, missing, mis-shaped, miscounted, wrong material or colour), else within tolerance (T-3153); owner ruling where the owner asked the build to depart from the picture (T-3236). A ticket whose ## Image gate names this building does not close while it is not \"matches\" (tools/image_gate.mjs)."
